## Method and Boundary

Read only the three bound inputs. Compare the author's existing answers and
derivations with the completed, frozen FIRST results and conditions. No source,
definition, image, answer key, or choice file was opened. No math computation,
new proof, validator, test, or rerun of the frozen 331 checks was performed.
No author or FIRST file was edited.

Map the author's `answers.main` in 967 and 968 to FIRST's `whole` task.
Accept exact decimal/rational notation, TeX bracing, and implicit versus
explicit multiplication. The answer field and derivation are reviewed
together; an expanded answer need not be duplicated in its derivation.
Separate restatements of natural domains and extra endpoint demonstrations
are not mandatory when the stipulated conditions are not changed.

All comparisons remain restricted to FIRST's original task conditions.
An even-power argument valid more generally does not authorize widening those
conditions. Principal square roots must remain nonnegative; no negative-root
branch is accepted. The zero endpoint in 969.a is included, while strict
endpoints and denominator zeros in the other affected tasks remain excluded.

